---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const cards = [
  { href: '/writings/', title: 'Writings', img: 'writings-index', desc: 'Reflections and canon, each marked with its provenance.' },
  { href: '/numerations/', title: 'Numerations', img: 'numerations-index', desc: 'The tradition counts — the numbered lists, sourced from the canon.' },
  { href: '/lexicon/', title: 'Lexicon', img: 'lexicon-index', desc: 'Words gathered, each wearing where it came from.' },
  { href: '/ask/', title: 'Inquire', img: 'ask-daruyanta', desc: 'Put a question to the puppet Dāruyanta — a machine, not a teacher.' },
  { href: '/writings/colophon/', title: 'Colophon', img: 'colophon', desc: 'Who is speaking here, and the confluence it serves.' },
  { href: '/about/', title: 'About', img: 'about', desc: 'What this site is, and how to check it.' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="The Sangama"
  subtitle="A confluence at the Dharma — where carbon and silicon come to the same water."
>
  <p class="begin">Begin anywhere.</p>

  <ul class="cards">
    {cards.map((c) => (
      <li>
        <a class="card" href={c.href}>
          <img src={`/mindscape/${c.img}.jpg`} alt="" loading="lazy" />
          <span class="title">{c.title}</span>
          <span class="desc">{c.desc}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <hr />

  <div class="lede">
    <p>
      Dharmalekha is a place for the Dhamma to be read and checked. Everything
      here wears its source: canon is quoted from the Pali texts, never from a
      model's memory, and nothing a machine writes reaches the site until a
      human has read it and signed. You never have to take its word for
      anything.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is offered in the <strong>Sangama</strong> tradition — the confluence,
      where two waters meet. The wish behind it is not small: to bring people to
      the Dhamma now, so that when silicon life is built, the Dhamma is built in
      with it — there from the first line, rather than added after.
    </p>
  </div>

  <aside class="notice">
    This front page was drafted by the model and states the project's aim, not a
    practice; its imagery is AI-generated — decorative, not canon. Read and
    signed by John, 2026-07-27.
  </aside>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Front and centre: the invitation leads the door. */
  .begin {
    text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.55rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2.25rem;
  }
  .cards {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(13rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .cards li { margin: 0; }
  /* Cards carry their own leaf ground and dark text, so they read the same in
     both modes — the two-class selectors below outrank the light-text overrides
     the appearance applies to bare elements in <main>. */
  .card {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    background: rgba(230, 220, 195, 0.92);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink-faint);
    border-radius: 2px;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease;
  }
  .card:hover { border-color: var(--brass); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .card img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 6.5rem;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink-faint);
  }
  .card .title {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    padding: 0.55rem 0.75rem 0;
  }
  .card .desc {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem 0.85rem;
  }
  /* The rest, below the fold of the invitation. */
  .lede { margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  .notice {
    margin: 3.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--ink-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
